@page "/"

<PageTitle>Clarity Belongs - Keep an eye on what matters</PageTitle>
<HeadContent>
    <meta name="description" content="Clarity Belongs monitors public websites, endpoints, certificates, domains, and DNS so you can review status and changes over time." />
</HeadContent>

<div class="shell public-shell">
    <section class="public-hero public-hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-copy">
            <div class="eyebrow">CLARITY BELONGS</div>
            <h1>Tell Clarity what matters. We keep an eye on it.</h1>
            <p class="public-lead">Monitor public websites, endpoints, certificates, domains, DNS records, and service status. Clarity checks them over time, saves what it observes, and shows you when the recorded result changes.</p>
            <div class="action-row public-actions">
                <AuthorizeView>
                    <Authorized>
                        <a class="button" href="/add">Watch something</a>
                        <a class="button secondary" href="/my-clarity">Open My Clarity</a>
                    </Authorized>
                    <NotAuthorized>
                        <a class="button" href="/signup">Start free</a>
                        <a class="button secondary" href="/products">See what Clarity can watch</a>
                    </NotAuthorized>
                </AuthorizeView>
            </div>
            <p class="microcopy">Start with five active follows for free. No card required.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-visual" aria-label="Example Clarity activity">
            <div class="hero-visual-topline">
                <span class="status-dot"></span>
                <span>Clarity is watching</span>
                <span class="hero-live-pill">Active</span>
            </div>
            <div class="hero-watch-card hero-watch-card-featured">
                <div class="watch-icon">↗</div>
                <div>
                    <small>Something changed</small>
                    <strong>Website content updated</strong>
                    <span>Change evidence saved</span>
                </div>
                <span class="watch-state changed">Changed</span>
            </div>
            <div class="hero-watch-card">
                <div class="watch-icon">✓</div>
                <div>
                    <small>Still healthy</small>
                    <strong>Public website</strong>
                    <span>Latest check succeeded</span>
                </div>
                <span class="watch-state healthy">Healthy</span>
            </div>
            <div class="hero-watch-card">
                <div class="watch-icon">◷</div>
                <div>
                    <small>Certificate status</small>
                    <strong>SSL expiration</strong>
                    <span>Expiration remains visible</span>
                </div>
                <span class="watch-state reminder">Tracked</span>
            </div>
            <p>One place to review what Clarity checked and what changed.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="public-section idea-section">
        <div class="section-intro">
            <div class="eyebrow">HOW IT WORKS</div>
            <h2>Choose the thing. Clarity keeps checking it.</h2>
            <p>Pick a supported public target, choose the watch that matches it, and Clarity records scheduled observations in your account.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-grid">
            <div><strong>1</strong><span>Choose what to watch</span></div>
            <div><strong>2</strong><span>Clarity checks it</span></div>
            <div><strong>3</strong><span>History builds</span></div>
            <div><strong>4</strong><span>Review what changed</span></div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="public-section monitor-section">
        <div class="section-heading">
            <div>
                <div class="eyebrow">WHAT CAN CLARITY WATCH?</div>
                <h2>Launch-ready monitoring for public internet targets.</h2>
            </div>
            <a href="/products">Browse all capabilities</a>
        </div>
        <div class="product-grid public-product-grid">
            <a class="product-card monitor-card" href="/products/website-uptime">
                <div class="monitor-icon">◎</div>
                <div class="eyebrow">AVAILABILITY</div>
                <h2>Website uptime</h2>
                <p>Record whether a public website or endpoint responds, including recovery after a failure.</p>
                <span class="monitor-link">See uptime monitoring →</span>
            </a>
            <a class="product-card monitor-card" href="/products/website-change">
                <div class="monitor-icon">↗</div>
                <div class="eyebrow">CONTENT</div>
                <h2>Website changes</h2>
                <p>Store whole-page content observations and review before-and-after evidence when the recorded page changes.</p>
                <span class="monitor-link">See website change monitoring →</span>
            </a>
            <a class="product-card monitor-card" href="/products/ssl-expiration">
                <div class="monitor-icon">◷</div>
                <div class="eyebrow">CERTIFICATES & DOMAINS</div>
                <h2>Expiration tracking</h2>
                <p>Keep certificate and domain expiration information visible alongside the rest of your monitoring history.</p>
                <span class="monitor-link">See expiration watches →</span>
            </a>
            <a class="product-card monitor-card" href="/products/dns-change">
                <div class="monitor-icon">≋</div>
                <div class="eyebrow">DNS</div>
                <h2>DNS changes</h2>
                <p>Record public address, nameserver, MX, SPF, DKIM, and DMARC answers and surface changes over time.</p>
                <span class="monitor-link">See DNS monitoring →</span>
            </a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="public-section split-callout">
        <div>
            <div class="eyebrow">MY CLARITY</div>
            <h2>Your follows and their history in one place.</h2>
            <p>My Clarity shows what you asked Clarity to watch, the latest status, recorded changes, and saved history.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mock-feed">
            <div><span class="badge">Changed</span><strong>Website content updated</strong><small>Evidence saved</small></div>
            <div><span class="badge">Recovered</span><strong>Website responding again</strong><small>Recovery recorded</small></div>
            <div><span class="badge">Healthy</span><strong>DNS answer unchanged</strong><small>Latest check succeeded</small></div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="public-section ecosystem-section">
        <div class="section-intro">
            <div class="eyebrow">HOW CLARITY FITS</div>
            <h2>Software Belongs helps you do. Clarity helps you know.</h2>
            <p>Software Belongs gives people useful tools. Clarity keeps watch over supported public targets that change over time. AutoPilot IT applies the same self-service philosophy to business technology.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ecosystem-grid">
            <a href="https://softwarebelongs.com"><strong>Software Belongs</strong><span>DO — useful tools that help you act.</span></a>
            <div class="ecosystem-current"><strong>Clarity Belongs</strong><span>KNOW — keep an eye on what matters.</span></div>
            <div><strong>AutoPilot IT</strong><span>HANDLE — self-service technology for business.</span></div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="public-cta">
        <div class="eyebrow">STOP CHECKING</div>
        <h2>Give Clarity something to keep an eye on.</h2>
        <p>Start with a supported website, endpoint, certificate, domain, DNS record, or service-status source.</p>
        <AuthorizeView>
            <Authorized>
                <a class="button" href="/add">Watch something</a>
            </Authorized>
            <NotAuthorized>
                <a class="button" href="/signup">Start free</a>
            </NotAuthorized>
        </AuthorizeView>
    </section>
</div>
